This is a REGULAR FILE on purpose. Do not delete it. Do not make it a directory.

OpenCode scans this directory (.opencode/agents/) recursively for *.md files and
registers each one as an agent. It separately bootstraps its plugins and goal
state into $PWD/.opencode/. If OpenCode is launched with a working directory of
.opencode/agents/, those two paths collide: the plugin dependency tree lands
inside the agent scan path and ~30 node_modules README.md / CHANGELOG.md files
get registered as phantom agents, polluting the Tab cycle.

Because this path is occupied by a regular file, that nested directory can no
longer be created. Launching OpenCode from the wrong directory now fails fast
with a BadResource error naming this path, instead of silently misbehaving.

The real fix is to always launch opencode from the repository root. See the
"OpenCode Agent System" section of AGENTS.md.
